    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac><mi>sin</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac><mi>cos</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mi>sin</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></math><br />Clearly, for options <math><mi>A</mi></math> and <math><mi>B</mi></math> <math><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is not injective and for option <math><mi>C</mi></math> <math><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is not surjective</p><p><math><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is bijective only for option <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>D</mi></math></p>",
